{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/k8s/postgres-dev/postgres.yaml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T01:06:57.772553Z","id":"6a989dbb755f204c0ee696dec18a2496c7b182861a115050a4cec2ebe6fe0535","body":{"detail":"Failure: `kubectl apply -k deploy/k8s/postgres-dev` after creating clax-secrets as the kustomization's comments say leaves the clax-postgres StatefulSet's pod in CreateContainerConfigError (secret \"clax-postgres-dev\" not found), and every fleet pod fails to connect to clax-postgres:5432 and crash-loops. postgres.yaml:60-62 has `envFrom: secretRef: name: clax-postgres-dev`, but commit 347050368 replaced the kustomization's `secretGenerator` (POSTGRES_USER=clax, POSTGRES_PASSWORD=clax-dev, POSTGRES_DB=clax) with the `patches` block (deploy/k8s/postgres-dev/kustomization.yaml:15-31); `grep -rn clax-postgres-dev deploy docs` finds only the reference. Without POSTGRES_PASSWORD the postgres:17 image also refuses to initialise, and without POSTGRES_USER/POSTGRES_DB the readiness probe's `pg_isready -U clax -d clax` and the documented URL postgresql://clax:clax-dev@clax-postgres:5432/clax name a role and database that do not exist. docs/kubernetes.md:189-192 and the kustomization's header (\"a password in this file\") still describe the generator.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":60},"end":{"line":68},"content_hash":"7e19f04e0a79486fce1fcb4ce3b3929e7a0fe266e250146617e459eff5ee03cc"},"suggested_fix":"Restore the secretGenerator beside the patches in deploy/k8s/postgres-dev/kustomization.yaml (name clax-postgres-dev, literals POSTGRES_USER=clax, POSTGRES_PASSWORD=clax-dev, POSTGRES_DB=clax). Add a test in crates/clax-fleet/src/main.rs that every secretRef name in deploy/k8s is either clax-secrets or generated by a kustomization.","summary":"postgres-dev's PostgreSQL reads its user, password and database from a Secret clax-postgres-dev that nothing creates, so the database pod never starts","tags":["review","review:k8s-deep-2","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/k8s/postgres-dev/postgres.yaml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:14.035555Z","id":"74e5437dec08bda7eb59ac132bc3c4141baa3d1cc25a295a4b927021b335fb9f","body":{"detail":"deploy/k8s/postgres-dev/postgres.yaml:60-62 is `envFrom: - secretRef: name: clax-postgres-dev`. `grep -rn clax-postgres-dev deploy docs` (excluding .qual) returns only deploy/k8s/postgres-dev/postgres.yaml:62. `git show 347050368 -- deploy/k8s/postgres-dev/kustomization.yaml` shows the removed lines `-secretGenerator: - name: clax-postgres-dev literals: POSTGRES_USER=clax, POSTGRES_PASSWORD=clax-dev, POSTGRES_DB=clax` replaced by `+patches:`. The current kustomization.yaml (lines 1-31) has resources ../postgres and postgres.yaml and only the patches block; its header (line 3) still says \"a password in this file\". A non-optional envFrom secretRef to a missing Secret leaves the container in CreateContainerConfigError, so the database never starts and the overlay as documented does not run.","kind":"comment","references":"6a989dbb755f204c0ee696dec18a2496c7b182861a115050a4cec2ebe6fe0535","summary":"confirmed: postgres.yaml reads Secret clax-postgres-dev, which nothing in deploy/k8s creates since 347050368","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/k8s/postgres-dev/postgres.yaml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T04:09:42.065132Z","id":"2cf7a7551eabcb29c0953d5f31ae0181208df9ea2d7b1956116383b0bcf64760","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e6b59f7af","summary":"postgres-dev's kustomization generates clax-postgres-dev again. Test: main.rs every_secret_the_manifests_read_is_created_or_documented. Evidence: `just ci` at e6b59f7af passes the clax-fleet, clax-pagevfs, scripts and manifest tests (357 of 361; the 4 failures are clax-server api_seats::load_150_people_on_100_seats and //apps/clax_app:apk_test, which fail on main too, and two web e2e lanes that passed when rerun alone). PostgreSQL tests are ignored without CLAX_TEST_PG_URL.","supersedes":"6a989dbb755f204c0ee696dec18a2496c7b182861a115050a4cec2ebe6fe0535","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
